│                                              │
│ The core issue is that the RadioSelect       │
│ widget incorrectly renders a blank option    │
│ ("---------") when a foreign key field is    │
│ present and blank=False. This is because the │
│ default rendering behavior of the            │
│ RadioSelect widget doesn't account for the   │
│ requirement of not displaying a blank option │
│ for required fields. The fix involves        │
│ modifying the render method within the       │
│ RadioSelect widget to prevent the generation │
│ of the blank option when the field is        │
│ required. Specifically, we need to ensure    │
│ that the RadioSelect widget doesn't include  │
│ an empty radio button option when the        │
│ associated field is not nullable.            │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]<./widgets/RadioSelect.py>[/file]     │
│  [original]def render(self, name, value,     │
│  attrs=None, choices=None):                  │
│      options = []                            │
│      for value, label in choices:            │
│          options.append((value, label))      │
│      options.append(('','---------'))        │
│      return mark_safe(                       │
│          '<ul id="id_%s">' % name            │
│          '<li>'                              │
│          '<label for="%s_0">' % name         │
│          '<input type="radio" id="%s_0"      │
│  name="%s" value="%s" ' % (name, name, valu  │
│          'checked="checked" %attrs>          │
│  ---------</label></li>' % (name, value)     │
│          '</ul>'                             │
│      )                                       │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]def render(self, name, value,      │
│  attrs=None, choices=None):                  │
