│ The core issue is that the RadioSelect       │
│ widget in Django’s forms is incorrectly      │
│ presenting an empty option ("-------") when  │
│ blank=False is specified for a foreign key   │
│ field. This happens because the widget       │
│ doesn't properly handle the case where a     │
│ valid foreign key value is not selected. The │
│ existing code checks for blank but doesn't   │
│ prevent the empty option from being rendered │
│ when a valid choice exists. The fix involves │
│ ensuring that the RadioSelect widget doesn't │
│ render an empty option when a valid foreign  │
│ key value is present. This can be achieved   │
│ by modifying the render method within the    │
│ RadioSelect widget to only render options    │
│ that have a value.                           │
│                                              │
